  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.rust.Rust`.\n\n**Obligations.** The requirement has two parts:\n1. The declared surface: `pub struct Rust;` with `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy` implementations.\n2. `Rust` supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the chapter. The refining requirements `sources.rust.language`, `sources.rust.items` and `sources.rust.fingerprints` carry the detail, so I judge only that `Rust` supplies those rules.\n\n**Declared surface.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` generates rustdoc. Through `check_declaration`, it compares the declaration in the book with rustdoc's published declaration.\n- It also asserts that the trait-impl list in the requirement text (`Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang`, `Copy`) equals rustdoc's trait impls for the page (`rustdoc.trait_impls(page)`). A missing or extra impl, including `Debug`, would fail it.\n- `Debug` has no behavioral test. The text states only that the impl exists, so the rustdoc comparison is the relevant check.\n\n**Behaviour.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` calls its helper `check` with `languages::Rust`, the file name `a.RS`, the source `fn check() {}`, the selector `fn[check]`, the extensions `[\"rs\"]` and the scheme `rust-structural-v1`. The helper is bounded by `OutlineLang + Default + Copy`.\n- It asserts the following:\n  - `extensions()` equals `[\"rs\"]`.\n  - `fingerprint_scheme()` equals `rust-structural-v1`.\n  - `Clone::clone` works.\n  - `L::default()` yields the same scheme.\n  - The type is zero-sized.\n  - Extension-based inference matches explicit language selection: the fingerprints are equal, and the selectors, diagnostic and root span match.\n  - `RS` matches case-insensitively.\n  - `select(\"fn[check]\")` succeeds.\n  - `search_structure` returns ranges.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[rust_items_attach_documentation_and_preserve_structural_hashes]` is also marked for `Rust`. It checks Rust selection and item spans, doc comments and attributes attached to items, and formatting-insensitive fingerprints that still change when the code changes.\n- Other tests, such as `bundled_structural_search_returns_matches_and_rejects_bad_rules_and_source` and `recovered_outlines_keep_the_diagnostic_and_intact_items`, use `languages::Rust` directly and support these checks.\n\nI found no uncovered obligation and no acknowledgments apply.",
